   "subject": "Line-transect Analysis - Segmented Transect question",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Hello-\r<br>\r<br>I am analyzing ship-based line transect data for Marine mammals, and have=\r<br> numerous transects (defined as a line  traversing the study site) that a=\r<br>re segmented, usually because poor weather or other constraints prevented=\r<br> us from completing them.  The study area is large (&gt;600,000 km 2) and mo=\r<br>st &#39;planned&#39; transects were several hundred km long, but in some cases on=\r<br>ly a fraction of these were presented.=20\r<br>\r<br>A related issue is that some of the completed  &#39;transects&#39; actually ended=\r<br> up being zig-zag courses within the study area.=20\r<br>\r<br>My questions are:\r<br>1) is there a minimum lenght (or proportion of planned transects) that sh=\r<br>ould be considered a transect when analyzing the data in Distance?\r<br>2) if yes to above, can I combine segments to make a transect of sufficen=\r<br>t length &#39;after the fact&#39;?\r<br>3) are there any issues with using zig-zag transects (assuming we can acc=\r<br>ount for re-sighting of the same individuals) as opposed to &#39;line&#39; transe=\r<br>ct, within in the study site (I define a &#39;zig-zag transect&#39; as a single t=\r<br>ransect that has a zig-zag pattern to it).\r<br>\r<br>\r<br>Thank you,\r<br>-Tom N.\r<br>\r<br>--\r<br>distance-sampling list home page:\r<br>  <a href=\"http://www.jiscmail.ac.uk/lists/distance-sampling.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.jiscmail.ac.uk/lists/distance-sampling.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792477516550000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2o-Q5w5HiV8b74QbqbQ_by\">http://www.jiscmail.ac.uk/lists/distance-sampling.html</a>\r<br>To unsubscribe, go to the home page and click &quot;Join or leave the list&quot;,\r<br>  or email <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">jisc...@jiscmail.ac.uk</a> with the following message body:\r<br>  leave distance-sampling\r<br>Before posting to the list, read the list guidelines at\r<br>  <a href=\"http://www.jiscmail.ac.uk/files/distance-sampling/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.jiscmail.ac.uk/files/distance-sampling/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792477516550000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3nYLIQ4UObT40lkgPAY0kk\">http://www.jiscmail.ac.uk/files/distance-sampling/</a>\r<br>    distance-sampling.welcome\r<br>Any questions, email the list owner at\r<br>  <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">distance-sam...@jiscmail.ac.uk</a>\r<br>--\r<br>"
    ]
